  "result": "Excellent! All 334 tests pass. Here's what I've added to src/money.js:\n\n## Foreign Currency Support\n\nAdded to `src/money.js`:\n\n**RATES** export:\n- `EUR: 1` (1 euro = 1 EUR)\n- `USD: 1.085` (1 euro = 1.085 USD)\n- `GBP: 0.8425` (1 euro = 0.8425 GBP)\n\n**convert(cents, currency)** function:\n- Takes an amount in euro cents and a currency code\n- Returns `{ ok: true, value: converted_cents }` for valid currencies\n- Returns `{ ok: false, error: 'UNKNOWN_CURRENCY' }` for unknown currencies\n- Properly rounds to the nearest cent\n- Handles negative amounts and zero\n\n**formatMoney(cents, currency)** function:\n- Formats amounts in the specified currency with proper symbols:\n  - `\u20ac` for EUR\n  - `$` for USD\n  - `\u00a3` for GBP\n- Applies the conversion rate automatically\n- Includes thousands separators and 2 decimal places\n- Handles negative amounts with minus sign prefix\n- Returns empty string for unknown currencies\n\nAdded 28 comprehensive tests covering:\n- RATES validation\n- EUR \u2194 USD conversion\n- EUR \u2194 GBP conversion\n- Unknown currency handling\n- Rounding behavior\n- Negative amounts and zero\n- Large amounts\n- Thousands separator formatting\n- Rate consistency\n- Edge cases (1 cent conversion)",
